    values:originalText "(9) If the person becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances where the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the Minister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament, within 15 sitting days of that House after the day the person becomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:  (a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under subsection (1A); and  (b) states the kind of work covered by paragraph (1)(a); and  (c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power, including why the Minister considers that engagement in that kind of work is of benefit to Australia." ;
    skos:definition "(9) If the person becomes an Australian citizen in circumstances where the Minister exercised the power under subsection (1A), the Minister must cause to be tabled in each House of the Parliament, within 15 sitting days of that House after the day the person becomes an Australian citizen, a statement that:  (a) states that the Minister has exercised the power under subsection (1A); and  (b) states the kind of work covered by paragraph (1)(a); and  (c) sets out the reasons for the Minister’s exercise of that power, including why the Minister considers that engagement in that kind of work is of benefit to Australia."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "54b326315aa0e365d7fe9f37d1f44dd0ffc05c88e49528306f0799f72b0d40aa" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-special-residence-requirements-act-2013-sch-1-sec-9 ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minister must provide statement to Parliament after granting citizenship in certain circumstances." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
